# Line endings: LF in the repository AND in every working copy, whatever a
# machine's core.autocrlf says. Prettier expects LF (its default), Vercel builds
# on Linux, and a Windows checkout in CRLF made `prettier --check` report every
# file as unformatted when none of them were. Binary files are detected and left
# alone by `text=auto`.
* text=auto eol=lf
